Fillets: a walk whose first point lies on a restriction within the guide's
tolerance ends there on the restriction, as from any later point
(mitcad#2018).

The bent guide of 1801 with its bend radius between 23.5 and 24.5: the
rounding of the outer sloped edge of the rib nearest each end starts its
walk 0.0024 from the spine's end, where the reframed first section's
contact on the rib's sloped side lies on that side's edge with the tube
(the side's lower edge, within 6e-5). The walk back towards the spine's
end left the face at its first step; BRepBlend_Walking::InternalPerform
takes any first step that leaves a face for a step too large and halves
it, down to the guide's tolerance, and then ends the walk at the first
point with no point on the restriction. ChFi3d's ComputeData took that for
a walk that drags (the first point 0.0024 from the spine's end, more than
ten times the guide's tolerance, on no restriction) and the rounding failed
("the walk between the two faces fails"). At 23 and 25 a halved step
happened to land inside the face, and the next step found the restriction.

- BRepBlend_Walking::InternalPerform: a first step that leaves a face is
  halved as before, except the last one the guide's tolerance allows (a
  step under twice that tolerance) where it leaves one face, the other's
  point inside its face: that step goes on to the reframing on the
  restriction, as a step from any later point does, and where that gives a
  point on the one restriction past the first point, the walk ends there.
  Otherwise (the reframing fails or gives the first point itself, as for a
  walk starting where an earlier one ended on that restriction) the step is
  halved as before. Taken at the first point itself, the walk looped
  without end in OCCT's case blend/encoderegularity/A1; taken where both
  points left their faces or the reframing failed, the corners of
  geometry.suite.fillet_corners (a vault's end rounded into the face it
  runs into) and geometry.fillet_still_ball_corners failed or hung.
- No catch is added.

Test: geometry.fillet_corner_walk_over_vertex (the case's second body) and
cli.fcstd_bend_reported (the bend radius set to 24).

